  "question": {
    "text": "On heating water, bubbles being formed at the bottom of the vessel detatch and rise. Take the bubbles to be spheres of radius R and making a circular contact of radius r with the bottom of the vessel. If r &lt;&lt; R, and the surface tension of water is T, value of r just before bubbles detatch is :<br />(density of water is <math> <mrow> <msub> <mi>&#961;</mi> <mtext>w</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math>)<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/EM0025730_Question.jpg\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 191px;\" />",
    "image": null
  },
